{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Pass before the people, etc.</b> Perhaps HaShem knew that the thirst among the people had grown severe and they would be in danger even in a short time; therefore He said that the moment he passes, he should pass before the people — meaning, in a manner that they know you are going to find water for them, so that the fire of thirst may subside among them in the meantime, and you shall not travel by a route that is not before them. And also take the elders with you, so that there be a palpable sense of it." "<b>With which you struck, etc.</b> And this will be a wondrous sign, for this very [staff] that spoiled the existing waters and turned them to blood will, through supernal power, perform an opposite action — that it bring forth water for the people to drink. And herein lie miraculous contradictions that confound those who scheme to deny, for they are the wonders of the God of Israel; with this staff the skull of one who thinks otherwise is shattered."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:09.728474663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}